Update fields on an existing Foundry routine.

Only the named flags change; all other fields are preserved verbatim.
To change the trigger or action type, delete and recreate the routine.

Usage
  azd ai routine update <name> [flags]

Flags
      --agent-endpoint-id string : New agent endpoint ID
      --agent-name string        : New project-scoped agent name
      --at string                : New ISO 8601 datetime (timer trigger only)
      --connection-id string     : New workspace connection ID (github-issue trigger only)
      --conversation-id string   : New conversation to continue (preview)
      --cron string              : New cron expression (recurring trigger only)
      --description string       : New description for the routine
      --event-name string        : New event name (custom trigger only)
      --file string              : Path to a YAML/JSON manifest; merged fields win unless overridden by flags
      --issue-event string       : New GitHub issue event: opened or closed (github-issue trigger only)
      --owner string             : New GitHub owner (github-issue trigger only)
      --parameters string        : New parameters JSON object (custom trigger only)
      --provider string          : New external provider (custom trigger only)
      --repository string        : New GitHub repository (github-issue trigger only)
      --session-id string        : New session to continue
      --time-zone string         : New time zone (recurring trigger only)

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string              : Sets the current working directory
      --debug                   : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string      : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help                    : help for update
      --no-prompt               : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string           : The output format (supported: json, table) (default "table")
  -p, --project-endpoint string : Foundry project endpoint URL for remote operations only (not add, context, or version)
      --timeout string          : HTTP request timeout override (for example, 2m or 90s). Defaults to 30s for reads and 2m0s for writes. Not supported by add, context, or version.

Examples
  Change the description while preserving other fields
    azd ai routine update nightly-summary --description "Summarize the day's activity"
